-- title:
--   Locally torsion at Eisenstein maximal ideals implies torsion
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let `JZero p` be the degree-zero divisor class group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the modular function field of level $p$ base-changed to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, carrying the commuting endomorphisms `heckeOperatorBar p` indexed by the primes. Assume: `hcomm`, that these endomorphisms commute pairwise; `hseam`, that the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{Z}}(\mathrm{JZero}\ p)$ generated by their range is finitely generated as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module; `hdiv`, that `JZero p` is divisible (every $x$ is $m\cdot y$ for some $y$, for every $m \neq 0$); and `htorsfin`, that the $n$-torsion of `JZero p` is finite for every $n > 0$. Equip `JZero p` with the `HeckeAlg`-module structure `heckeModuleBar p`, where `HeckeAlg` $= \mathbb{Z}[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ acts through `heckeEvalBar hcomm`. Then for every element $z$ of the additive subgroup of the quotient `EisensteinQuotient p` $=$ `JZero p` modulo `eisensteinKernel (JZero p) (eisensteinIdeal p) • ⊤` generated by `eisensteinQuotientRational p`, the image of $\{x : \forall \sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}),\ \sigma\cdot x - x \in$ that submodule$\}$: if for every prime $q$ there is $s \in$ `HeckeAlg` with $q \nmid$ `eisensteinEval p` $s$ (i.e. $s \notin$ `eisensteinMaximalIdeal p q`) and $s\cdot z$ of finite additive order, then $z$ has finite additive order. The proof uses neither `hdiv` and `htorsfin` nor the hypothesis that $z$ lies in the subgroup generated by `eisensteinQuotientRational p`.
--
--   This is the support step in Mazur's analysis of the Eisenstein quotient: torsion of an element of the quotient of $J_0(p)$ by the Eisenstein kernel may be tested at the maximal ideals $\mathfrak{J} + (q)$ of the Hecke algebra alone, $q$ running over the primes. It feeds the assembly of the finiteness statement for the rational points of the Eisenstein quotient, [`ModularCurve.eisensteinQuotientRational_isTorsion_heckeModuleBar`](thm.html#ModularCurve.eisensteinQuotientRational_isTorsion_heckeModuleBar).
-- source:
